      <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="biger" data-hint="Big has a one-syllable consonant-vowel-consonant spelling with a short stressed vowel, so double g." data-fix="Cedar is bigger than Pine." data-why="The comparative of big is spelled bigger with double g." data-success-message="Correct. You applied the precise final-consonant doubling condition.">
      <h3>Repair one high-risk spelling</h3><p>The table note says, “Cedar is biger than Pine.” Tap the word to repair.</p>
      <div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="cedar">Cedar</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="is">is</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="biger">biger</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="pine">than Pine.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>
    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Thirty-second retrieval</h3>
      <p>Without looking back, give one comparative with an explicit reference, one superlative with a defined set, one equality frame, one exact difference, one possessive superlative, and one tied-extreme sentence.</p>
